# Implementation Plan: Wallet Module (Buyer & Farmer Dashboard)

This document outlines the architectural strategy for the unified Wallet Module, providing both Buyers and Farmers with a state-of-the-art dashboard to monitor their Arbitrum Sepolia activity, escrow states, and financial analytics.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Wallet Connection & Live Data:** Since this is a browser-based sandbox environment, the actual `window.ethereum` MetaMask provider will not be injected. I will build the Wallet Dashboard to automatically fallback to simulated wallet states (e.g., generating mock ETH balances and transaction histories derived from your existing MongoDB Orders collection).
> **Analytics Charts:** I will implement the analytics charts using beautiful Tailwind-based CSS bar charts to avoid introducing heavy external charting libraries (like Recharts) that could slow down the Vite build.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Rust + Axum + MongoDB)
#### [NEW] [backend/src/models/transaction.rs](file:///c:/Users/akshar%20Patel/Agrichain/backend/src/models/transaction.rs)
- Define a unified `Transaction` schema to represent blockchain events (Payment, Escrow Lock, Escrow Release).

#### [NEW] [backend/src/controllers/wallet.rs](file:///c:/Users/akshar%20Patel/Agrichain/backend/src/controllers/wallet.rs)
- Create a dedicated controller for all wallet endpoints:
  - `GET /api/wallet/balance`: Calculate mock locked ETH (from active Escrows) and return available balance.
  - `GET /api/wallet/transactions`: Dynamically generate a transaction ledger by scanning the `orders` collection for the requested wallet address (capturing both "Lock" and "Release" events).
  - `GET /api/wallet/orders-paid`: Fetch orders where `buyer_wallet == address`.
  - `GET /api/wallet/orders-received`: Fetch orders where `farmer_id == address`.
  - `GET /api/wallet/analytics`: Aggregate monthly spending/earnings and order counts.

#### [NEW] [backend/src/routes/wallet.rs](file:///c:/Users/akshar%20Patel/Agrichain/backend/src/routes/wallet.rs)
- Register the new endpoints and export them to `backend/src/routes/mod.rs` under `/api/wallet`.

